# Line endings (change windows-build): the tree is LF everywhere, also in a Windows checkout.
# Byte-exact fixtures (.otio goldens, .kt projects) are read and compared as bytes, and git on a
# Windows runner converts to CRLF by default (core.autocrlf=true) — they would go red there.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touched by the conversion
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.db binary
*.db-shm binary
*.db-wal binary
*.7z binary
*.zip binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.flac binary
*.m4a binary
*.ogg binary
*.jpg binary

# Upstream OpenTimelineIO samples are kept byte for byte as published (some are CRLF)
src/fixtures/otio-samples/** -text
